
<% content_for :title, "Relapse Plans | Bipolar Sober" %>



<main class="relapse-hub">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="relapse-hub-hero">
    <div class="relapse-hub-container">

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO THE TOOLBOX",
          toolbox_path,
          class: "relapse-hub-back" %>

      <p class="relapse-hub-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / RELAPSE PLANS
      </p>

      <h1>
        MAKE A PLAN.<br>
        YOUR BRAIN<br>
        HAS OTHER IDEAS.
      </h1>

      <p class="relapse-hub-intro">
        Different triggers. Different plans.
        Pick what's happening.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- YOUR INTRODUCTION -->
  <section class="relapse-hub-note">
    <div class="relapse-hub-container">

      <p class="relapse-hub-label">
        01 / BEFORE THE BARGAINING STARTS
      </p>

      <h2>
        A LITTLE<br>
        PREPARATION.
      </h2>

      <div class="relapse-hub-copy">
        <p>
          Relapse doesn't always start with a drink.
          Sometimes it starts with an argument,
          a sleepless night, a pain flare,
          or an ordinary afternoon when
          you want to feel something different.
        </p>

        <p>
          These plans are for recognizing what's
          happening before alcohol starts looking
          like a reasonable solution.
          Each one addresses a different situation,
          the warning signs that come with it,
          and what you can do next.
        </p>

        <p>
          You don't need to wait until you're
          seriously considering drinking to use one.
          The point is to have a plan before
          your judgment, mood, or circumstances
          make following it more difficult.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- PLAN DIRECTORY -->
  <section class="relapse-hub-plans">
    <div class="relapse-hub-container">

      <div class="relapse-hub-heading">

        <p class="relapse-hub-label">
          02 / PICK YOUR PLAN
        </p>

        <h2>
          WHAT'S GOING<br>
          ON RIGHT NOW?
        </h2>

        <p>
          You can need more than one. There's no prize
          for making this shit fit neatly into a box.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="relapse-hub-grid">

        <!-- MANIA -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_mania_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-pink" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            01 / MANIA &amp; HYPOMANIA
          </p>

          <h3>
            BRAIN<br>
            WON'T<br>
            SHUT UP?
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            Racing thoughts, reduced sleep,
            excessive confidence, impulsive spending,
            and the temptation to drink
            when everything feels possible.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- DEPRESSION -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_depression_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-purple" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            02 / DEPRESSION
          </p>

          <h3>
            WHEN<br>
            EVERYTHING<br>
            FEELS HEAVY.
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            Months of exhaustion, isolation,
            hopelessness, and wanting alcohol
            to make you feel something different.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- MIXED SYMPTOMS -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_mixed_symptoms_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-yellow" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            03 / MIXED SYMPTOMS
          </p>

          <h3>
            WIRED.<br>
            MISERABLE.<br>
            NOW WHAT?
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            Depressive thoughts, manic agitation,
            racing thoughts, impulsivity,
            and the overwhelming desire
            to make it all stop.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- IMPULSIVITY -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_impulsivity_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-black" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            04 / IMPULSIVITY
          </p>

          <h3>
            BEFORE<br>
            "FUCK IT"<br>
            TAKES OVER.
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            The urge, the justification,
            the decision. Creating space
            between wanting something
            and acting on it.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- CHRONIC PAIN -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_chronic_pain_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-yellow" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            05 / CHRONIC PAIN
          </p>

          <h3>
            IT HURTS.<br>
            YOU WANT<br>
            A BREAK.
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            Sciatica, nerve pain, limited mobility,
            and the temptation to turn to alcohol
            when your body won't cooperate.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- BOREDOM -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_boredom_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-pink" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            06 / BOREDOM &amp; RESTLESSNESS
          </p>

          <h3>
            BORED<br>
            OUT OF YOUR<br>
            SKULL?
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            Empty evenings, restless energy,
            missing the excitement of drinking,
            and finding something else
            worth doing.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- ANGER -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_anger_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-purple" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            07 / ANGER &amp; CONFLICT
          </p>

          <h3>
            PISSED OFF.<br>
            STILL<br>
            SOBER.
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            Arguments, resentment, irritability,
            and wanting a drink because
            someone or something
            pushed you too far.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- LONELINESS -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_loneliness_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-yellow" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            08 / LONELINESS &amp; ISOLATION
          </p>

          <h3>
            JUST YOU<br>
            AND YOUR<br>
            LOUD BRAIN.
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            Drinking alone, withdrawing
            from people, missing connection,
            and recognizing when solitude
            becomes isolation.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- SOCIAL PRESSURE -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_social_pressure_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-black" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            09 / SOCIAL PRESSURE &amp; CELEBRATIONS
          </p>

          <h3>
            EVERYONE'S<br>
            DRINKING.<br>
            AND?
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            Parties, celebrations, unwanted offers,
            missing social drinking, and knowing
            when it's time to leave.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>


        <!-- AFTER DRINKING -->
        <%= link_to relapse_plan_after_drinking_path,
            class: "relapse-hub-card relapse-hub-card-pink" do %>

          <p class="relapse-hub-number">
            10 / AFTER DRINKING
          </p>

          <h3>
            I DRANK.<br>
            WHAT THE<br>
            FUCK NOW?
          </h3>

          <p class="relapse-hub-description">
            You drank. Now what?
            Stop the sequence, address
            the consequences, get support,
            and decide what happens next.
          </p>

          <span class="relapse-hub-cta">
            OPEN THE PLAN →
          </span>

        <% end %>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- PERSONAL NOTES -->
  <section class="relapse-hub-footer">
    <div class="relapse-hub-container">

      <p class="relapse-hub-label">
        03 / MAKE IT YOURS
      </p>

      <h2>
        YOUR PATTERNS.<br>
        YOUR PEOPLE.<br>
        YOUR PLAN.
      </h2>

      <div class="relapse-hub-copy">

        <p>
          Your warning signs won't always
          look the same. Sometimes the problem
          is your mood. Sometimes it's pain,
          boredom, loneliness, or a situation
          you didn't expect.
        </p>

        <p>
          Know what tends to happen before
          you want to drink. Know who you
          can contact, what helps you pause,
          and when you need more support
          than a self-help exercise can provide.
        </p>

        <p>
          A relapse plan isn't a guarantee
          that you'll never drink again.
          It's a way to make your next
          decision more deliberate,
          especially when your brain
          is making a convincing argument
          for doing something else.
        </p>

      </div>
<!-- BACK TO TOOLBOX -->
<nav class="index-home-nav" aria-label="Return to toolbox">
  <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
      toolbox_path,
      class: "index-home-button" %>
</nav>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
